            "summary": "(Reuters) -Hewlett Packard Enterprise forecast annual profit below Wall Street expectations on Wednesday, as it shifts its server business toward artificial intelligence and networking following its Juniper Networks acquisition.  Starting in the first quarter of fiscal 2026, the company will merge its server, hybrid cloud and financial services business segments into a newly created segment: cloud & AI.  HPE is targeting growth in the booming artificial intelligence infrastructure market, as businesses ramp up hardware and software spending to support AI.",
